=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTATION_DEFINITION_CHANGED
title: Changing the input column beside a kept answer relabels the test's data
origin: FP guard — only columns the expectation actually consumes count
note: reclassified 2026-09-21 (issue #93 contract decision, estate T-436,
note2: DECISIONS D-060): the expectation column is untouched, but the only
note3: tested input vanished beside a new one carrying the same answer —
note4: SUBJECT_INPUT_CHANGED's table spelling. Still silent for
note5: EXPECTATION_DEFINITION_CHANGED, which is what this guard exists for.
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [([50.0, 50.0], 105.0)],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, 0.05) == expected
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [([60.0, 45.0], 105.0)],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, 0.05) == expected
